i dont see git tab in step 2

Common snag. The Git tab only appears if RStudio can find a git installation and the project is git-enabled. Let me get you unstuck, there are a couple of likely causes.

First, check whether RStudio knows where git is:

RStudio → Tools → Global Options → Git/SVN. Look at the "Git executable" field.

If it's empty, that's the problem, RStudio can't find git. You'd browse to it (typically C:\Program Files\Git\bin\git.exe).
If it's filled in, git is found and the issue is the project itself (see below).
If the path is empty and you're not sure git is installed at all, check in a terminal:

git --version
Prints a version → git's installed, RStudio just needs pointing at it (fill in the path above).
"not recognized" → git isn't installed. Download Git for Windows from git-scm.com, install with defaults, restart RStudio.
If git IS found but there's still no Git tab, the project isn't git-initialised yet. Two ways to fix:

Option A (in RStudio): Tools → Version Control → Project Setup → set "Version control system" to Git → it'll offer to initialise and ask to restart the project. After restart, the Git tab appears.

Option B (terminal, then reopen): in your wildtag.ai folder:

cd /d "C:\Users\css6\Dropbox\W\wildtag.ai"
git init
Then in RStudio close and reopen the project (or Tools → Project Options → Git/SVN → set to Git). The tab appears once the folder has a .git directory.

Tell me what you find at the Tools → Global Options → Git/SVN screen (is the Git executable path filled in or empty?), and what git --version prints in a terminal. Those two answers pin down exactly which fix you need, and I'll walk you through just that one rather than guessing.

